    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "542:2209",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Park",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Park"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Sunday in the Park\n\nEvery Sunday, my family and I go to the park near our neighbourhood. It is a large green space with something for everyone.\n\nThe children head straight to the playground, where there are swings, slides, and a climbing frame. My younger sister loves the seesaw, while my brother prefers the monkey bars. There is soft ground under the equipment, so it is safe if they fall.\n\nMy parents usually sit on a bench near the pond. The pond has ducks and sometimes small fish. There is a wooden bridge across it and a narrow path that goes around the water.\n\nI like to jog on the running track that circles the park. There is also a cycling lane next to it for people on bicycles. Near the entrance, there is a water fountain where joggers stop to drink.\n\nIn the centre of the park, there is a large open field where families have picnics on blankets. Some people play football or throw a frisbee. There are tall trees that give shade, and flower beds with roses and lavender along the main path.\n\nThe park also has a small café near the car park, public toilets, and a few rubbish bins placed around the paths. I always feel relaxed after a visit.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "A Sunday in the Park Every Sunday, my family and I go to the park near our neighbourhood. It is a large green space with something for everyone. The children head straight to the playground, where there are swings, slides, and a climbing frame. My younger sister loves the seesaw, while my brother prefers the monkey bars. There is soft ground under the equipment, so it is safe if they fall. My parents usually sit on a bench near the pond. The pond has ducks and sometimes small fish. There is a wooden bridge across it and a narrow path that goes around the water. I like to jog on the running track that circles the park. There is also a cycling lane next to it for people on bicycles. Near the entrance, there is a water fountain where joggers stop to drink. In the centre of the park, there is a large open field where families have picnics on blankets. Some people play football or throw a frisbee. There are tall trees that give shade, and flower beds with roses and lavender along the main path. The park also has a small café near the car park, public toilets, and a few rubbish bins placed around the paths. I always feel relaxed after a visit."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. What do the children do when they arrive at the park?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. What do the children do when they arrive at the park?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. What can you see at the pond?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. What can you see at the pond?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What does the writer like to do in the park?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What does the writer like to do in the park?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. Where do families have picnics?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. Where do families have picnics?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. What facilities does the park have near the car park?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. What facilities does the park have near the car park?"
        }
      ]
    },
    "idioms-phrases": {
      "nodeId": "542:2222",
